{"duration_api_ms":81947,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"de827c0e-8cf4-4a5d-8c15-47ab53d22d5d","total_cost_usd":0.7763616000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":26,"cache_creation_input_tokens":63031,"cache_read_input_tokens":568848,"output_tokens":7912,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":777},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":63031,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":860,"cache_read_input_tokens":64790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4221},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":26,"outputTokens":7912,"cacheReadInputTokens":568848,"cacheCreationInputTokens":63031,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7763616000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":777,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_015D1jzNTVrc6gZ5XnTmjx7b","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/samples/wp68-dotnet; ls -R src/DcaShop.Product | grep -v '^$' | head -120; find . -name 'seed-catalogue.json' -not -path './node_modules/*' | grep -v /bin/ | grep -v /obj/; find src tests -path '*Views*' -iname '*product*' | grep -v /bin/ | grep -v /obj/","description":"List Product context files and views"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":22,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I planned CAT-01, but the plan stops at a question for you: one part of the story doesn't match what the shop actually does.\n\nThe story is marked `adopted`, which means it claims to describe existing behaviour, so nothing gets built. Four of its five scenarios match the code. The fifth, `catalogue-page-heading`, doesn't:\n- The heading \"Our Products\" and the breadcrumb \"Home / Products\" match.\n- The browser tab title is **\"Products\"**, not \"Product Catalog\" as the story says. It's set in `src/DcaShop.Web/Views/Product/Catalog.cshtml:2`, and `_Layout.cshtml:9` shows it unchanged.\n\nA scenario the code doesn't show can't be adopted, so I wrote decision record `.agents/factory/decisions/CAT-01-01.md` with three options:\n1. **Fix the story** to say \"Products\". This is my recommendation, unless the Java sample's catalogue template shows \"Product Catalog\". If it does, the two samples already disagree.\n2. **Change the shop** to \"Product Catalog\". The story would then stop being an adoption and become a change, with the Java sample kept in step.\n3. **Drop the title** from the scenario.\n\nFor each scenario, the plan in `tasks/CAT-01/plan.md` records where the behaviour lives and which test covers it:\n\n| Scenario | Planned test type | Existing test |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `catalogue-lists-the-seeded-range` (happy path) | browser (Playwright) | `SeededCatalogE2eTest` checks the count of 21 |\n| `catalogue-is-in-name-order` | integration | covered by the same browser test and a unit test (`InMemoryProductRepositoryTest`); no integration test |\n| `card-shows-name-description-and-image` | integration | none |\n| `card-leads-to-the-product` | integration | only partly: `ShopFlowTest` follows the first link, nothing checks every card or the link text |\n| `catalogue-page-heading` | integration | none |\n\nAdopting doesn't add tests, so those gaps stay recorded in the plan and nothing fills them.\n\nOne more thing to know: the story names a `seed-catalogue.json` file, but this repository doesn't have one. The 21 products are written directly in `SampleDataSeeder`. That file probably belongs to the specification, which I didn't read because it's outside this stage's input.\n\nI didn't run the story gate or any other stage.","ttft_ms":3177,"type":"result","duration_ms":82461,"uuid":"8f5f9d59-d290-49e9-9c0d-b672fc7453d1","ttft_stream_ms":2079,"time_to_request_ms":86,"first_content_frame_ms":2079,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
